# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend environment
#
# Copy to client/.env for local development. On Netlify, set the same keys in the
# site's build environment.
#
# IMPORTANT: every VITE_ value is inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD time,
# not read at runtime. Two consequences:
#   1. Never put a secret here. Only values that are safe to make public.
#   2. Changing one in Netlify requires a REDEPLOY to take effect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the API. Required — there is no runtime discovery of the API host,
# so an unset value falls back to http://localhost:4000 and every request from a
# deployed build fails.
#   production   https://score-and-scale-api.onrender.com
#   development  http://localhost:4000
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Supabase Storage, used for document uploads.
#
# The anon (publishable) key is designed to be public and is governed by Row
# Level Security. On its own it cannot write to the documents bucket: every
# upload needs a short-lived signed token that only the API can issue, and only
# after it has verified the enrollment belongs to the caller.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=documents

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google sign-in needs no frontend variable.
#
# The authorization-code flow runs entirely server-side: the button is a plain
# link to /api/auth/google on the backend, so no Google client id is exposed in
# this bundle and no Google SDK is shipped to the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time guard
#
# With VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY unset, Vite inlines them as
# compile-time constants, the guard clause in src/lib/supabaseClient.ts becomes
# statically true, and Rollup dead-code eliminates supabase-js out of the bundle
# entirely — producing a deploy where document upload can never work.
#
# vite.config.ts prints a warning when that happens. Treat it as a failed build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
